  "articleSummary": "The article argues that AI agents are useless without integration with real business systems, and that the Model Context Protocol (MCP) solves this by standardizing tool connections—much like USB-C standardized cables. The author presents a tutorial-style walkthrough using the Mastra framework, demonstrating how to configure MCP clients for local and remote services (e.g., Google Maps, weather APIs) and connect them to agents with minimal code. A key security point is per-user authentication to avoid shared credentials and quota issues. The intended audience is developers building production AI agents, with recurring metaphors of \"hands\" for integrations and USB-C for standardization.",
